+# Garage washing animation
+
+Owner request, 2026-10-14. GWA01: show washing at the actual touched car surface. GWA02: animate scrubbing, suds and falling water while retaining progressive cleaning and mouse/touch controls. GWA03: bound resources and clear feedback on miss, cancellation, orbit, Done, navigation, hiding, car replacement and teardown. Existing CW13/CW15/CW16, V06/G01/R01/Q01 remain applicable.
+
+The existing closest-triangle picker now returns its original condition coordinate plus the actual world contact and outward normal. The same nearest hit still feeds the original wash operation and swipe interpolation. A small closed beveled sponge with a fabric finish and rubber back rocks against that patch. Short-lived ivory suds and pale water droplets emerge there and shrink away. Releasing stops the sponge immediately; remaining particles drain in under one second. Background holds create neither cleaning nor contact feedback. The hover guide remains a quiet ring; no new instructions or player-facing controls were added.
+
+The effect is prepared lazily on the first Wash action, outside the car model. It reuses two fixed MultiMeshes (24 suds and 32 droplets), two small sponge parts and existing native finish shaders. Four extra geometry draws per existing view are active only during feedback; no shadow casters, texture assets, car-material replacements, new viewport or reflection passes are added. The original floor/deck captures include the effect through their existing layers. Slot-index sequences avoid touching global RNG state. Turning/zooming, cancellation, leaving Care, hiding and changing the car clear transient geometry; normal teardown frees it. Cleaning rates, wash volume, local condition schema/saves, actual car/kit/livery/condition, retained room/camera and canonical driving/scoring remain unchanged.
+
+Actual native evidence: [Compatibility door](evidence/garage-wash-animation-2026-10-14/gl_compatibility/washing-door.png), [Mobile door](evidence/garage-wash-animation-2026-10-14/mobile/washing-door.png), [cleaned patch](evidence/garage-wash-animation-2026-10-14/gl_compatibility/cleaned-patch.png). Each renderer also has real contact captures for the Pickup, Classic, Formula and Kart. [Compatibility animation](evidence/garage-wash-animation-2026-10-14/gl_compatibility/washing-animation.png) and [Mobile animation](evidence/garage-wash-animation-2026-10-14/mobile/washing-animation.png) are lossless APNGs assembled from 72 actual native frames. Production updates were stepped at 30 Hz for review; these previews are not performance measurements.
+
+All native checks use pinned `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf` via `scripts/dev.ps1`, with APPDATA redirected into `build/garage-wash-animation-user`. Independent local records are used; owner data and backend requests are not used. Actual commands:
+
+```powershell
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File build/run_garage_wash_animation.ps1
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File build/run_garage_wash_animation.ps1 -Renderer mobile
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File build/run_garage_wash_animation.ps1 -Check test_car_wash
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File build/run_garage_wash_animation.ps1 -Check test_car_wash -Renderer mobile
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File build/run_garage_wash_animation.ps1 -Check test_script_parse -Headless
+python build/encode_garage_wash_animation.py
+python build/checkpoint_garage_wash_animation.py
+```
+
+Final animation checks: 139 Compatibility and 139 Mobile/Vulkan, zero failures, including contact alignment, scrub/droplet motion, real cleaning, no background work, fixed pool reuse, input cancellation/orbit, local exact serialized condition persistence, navigation/hiding and release. Existing washing lifecycle/persistence/real-app tests: 1,402 per renderer, zero failures. The original blue-paint pixel assertion is retained; the new transient sponge is hidden alongside the old cursor only for the underlying paint comparison. Native blue channels rise 0.0824→0.2510 Compatibility and 0.1216→0.2627 Mobile. Project parse: 754 scripts, zero failures. Logs are under each renderer's `logs/` directory; existing regression captures are isolated under `existing-wash/`.
+
+Initial attempts are not counted as passes. Direct PowerShell execution hit the host execution policy; the established process-scoped Bypass runner resolves it. Normal user-log access was blocked until APPDATA was isolated. Restricted startup then could not read Windows certificates; automatically approved native runs resolve that startup dependency, and the verified stalled test process was stopped. A test fixture initially referenced a nonexistent clean-condition helper; it now uses the existing weathering snapshot. Two initial diagnostic failures used an already-expired droplet slot and compared pre/post JSON float representations; the final checks inspect the whole live pool and exact serialized save contents. A concurrent new CompactFrontLamps class briefly blocked the existing test; the normal native Import refresh completed and both original regressions subsequently passed. An optional preview attempt lacked Pillow; the final lossless encoder uses only Python's standard library and adds no dependency. Concurrent car geometry and showroom subpixel rounding edits are retained and excluded from this task's scoped checkpoint.
+
+Runtime files: `game/ui/car_showroom.gd`, new `game/ui/garage_wash_effect.gd` (+UID). Tests: new `game/tests/test_garage_wash_animation.gd` (+UID) and existing `game/tests/test_car_wash.gd` (isolated evidence argument and transient-feedback hiding for the original pixel assertion). Supporting runner/encoder/checkpoint live in `build/`; instructions/status/plan have the task follow-up. The isolated two-commit Git checkpoint and task-only patch preserve the main repository index/branch and unrelated edits.
+
+Owner appearance and physical-phone touch/frame-pacing acceptance remain. Manual review: enter Garage → Care → Wash, hold or swipe over each panel/wheel, move off the car, release, turn with two fingers/right mouse, switch sections/car, leave/reopen and confirm local washed areas persist. No phone test/attachment check, APK export/install/deployment, backend write, full Validate or physics merge was performed. Desktop Mobile/Vulkan is not a phone performance measurement.
